Z||000000||Sage||03-30-2000||12:00 PM||||Here is some food for thought;<BR>To everyone at the forum, I extend apologies to any that may have been offended by my "God bless America" thread. (This was some time ago, I'm sure some of you remember it, Patrick?)  I like the forum very much.  I visit here nearly every day, and find it an invaluable source of information and support. <BR>     I will refrain from posting much, as there are enough resident experts to answer most questions that come up, and as Phil has advised, "Never pass up an opportunity to shut up." I just found something that I wanted to share as it kind of summerizes my perspective.  It is like the tv tho, if you don't like what's on, change the channel, or turn it off. <BR>     Anyway, here goes;<P>           RULES FOR BEING HUMAN<BR>You will receive a body.<BR>You may like it or hate it,<BR>but it's yours to keep<BR>for the entire period.<P>You will learn lessons.<BR>You are enrolled in a full-time,<BR>informal school called life.<P>There are no mistakes, only lessons.<BR>Growth is a process of trial, error and<BR>experimentation.  The "failed" experiments<BR>are as much a part of the process as the experiments that ultimately "work"<P>Lessons are repeated until they are learned.<BR>A lesson will be presented to you<BR>in various forms until you<BR>learned it.  When you have learned it,<BR>you can go on to the next lesson.<P>Learning lessons does not end.<BR>There is no part of life that doesn't<BR>contain it's lessons.  If you're alive,<BR>there are still lessons to be learned.<P>"There" is no better than "here".<BR>When your "there" has become<BR>"here", you will simply obtain<BR>another "there" that will again<BR>look better than "here".<P>Other people are merely mirrors of<BR>you.  You can not love or hate<BR>something about another person<BR>unless it reflects to you something<BR>you love or hate about yourself.<P>What you make of your life is up to you.<BR>You have all the tools<BR>and resources you need.  What you<BR>do with them is up to you.<BR>The choice is yours.<P>          -- Anonymous --<P>I will not argue about any points raised here, there is nothing to argue.  I am merely putting it out as "food for thought".  Those that aren't hungry, don't have any!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000001||Patrick||03-30-2000||04:23 PM||||<BR>You're right, there's nothing to argue about in that post. Very nice.<P>Sage, you've confused me a bit with your reference to a <I>God bless America</I> thread. I recall no such thread. Are you referring to the post of yours where you exclaimed "This is America...", and I proceeded to remind you that this is an international forum? Hey, I'm not arguing, I'm just asking! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P> ||||reg||14
Z||000002||william_thorniii||03-30-2000||09:37 PM||||Sage,<P>Sadly, I hadn't realized you were missing until I saw this topic.  When I looked at the name of the originator... I thought "Hey, I haven't seen anything from him in a while!"  It is good to have you back... <P>There are quite a few whose presence has been lost in the last few months.  It seems that we have reaced a calm part for a while here on the Forum.  I don't think that anyone is as glad to see that as I am.  Hopefully we have learned our "lessons" from the last few months...<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||10
